 "answer": "On a GPU with 12 GiB of VRAM, Ollama should default to a **4,096-token** context window (4k).\n\nI believe Ollama sets this default by VRAM tier: under 24 GiB gets 4k, 24 GiB to under 48 GiB gets 32k, and 48 GiB or more gets 256k. I'm not certain of the exact release where this tiering was introduced, so check your version's documentation or release notes if the exact value matters.\n\nYou can override the default with the `OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH` environment variable or the `num_ctx` option in a request or Modelfile, though larger contexts need more memory.",
